+# Wave-4 LZ lane landed without breaking rc3 frames (review40/R01, claim `klz-w4-compat`)
+
+Branch `review40/R01`, on top of codec 32 (`benchmark/review40/klzh2/RESULTS.md`). The lane
+`origin/claude/w4-lz-20261118` (six commits and one merge ahead of rc3 `5071f388`) could not merge: it rewrote the
+block format of codec 28 in place, so a frame written by rc3 with `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz` in `speed` mode stopped
+decoding. This file records how it was landed, the compatibility proof and the numbers of the landed tree.
+
+**Sizes are exact; speeds are indicative only** (shared 4-vCPU VM, load average 1.5 to 2.4 during these runs, timed
+runs one at a time through the pass's `tools/measure.py`).
+
+## 1. What was done
+
+| lane commit | on this branch | change made while landing |
+|---|---|---|
+| `59f117f1` decmap: khuf one decode table and byte-table bit reversal, KLZH decoder one validation pass and fewer refills, x86 AVX2 word decoder | `8eca114d`, cherry-picked whole | none in `src`; the bindings' copies come from this branch |
+| `0dc7a8b1` KLZ stream format in place of codec 28 | `27e419dc`, ported | the lane's coder is **KLZS, codec 31** (`kolmo_klzs_*`); rc3's KLZ encoder and decoder stay under **28**, untouched; `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz` maps the LZ4 roles to 31; tests with blocks written by the rc3 sources |
+| `d9e86fa5` KLZH parse: single table at level 1, second recent offset after each match, `__builtin_memcpy` | `5cbef394`, cherry-picked | the parse call sits in `kzh_parse`, shared by codecs 29 and 32; the test that pinned KLZH's bytes to rc3's became a decode test of rc3's blocks |
+| `776ac3c3` bindings, SPEC, changelog, scripts | `f03fe76e` | SPEC rows: 28 = rc3's format, 31 = the lane's; changelog entry corrected; `run_all.sh` asks for `klzs1` |
+| `75d8a512`, `3a027805` the lane's RESULTS.md and ledger rows | `fba08c05`, `1fe6a718` | the lane's CODECS row for its "codec 28" is filed under 31; errata beside the lane's results (`benchmark/w4/lz/ERRATA-20261124.md`) |
+
+The landed `src/algo/klz.c` was compared with the lane's: the KLZS section is the lane's KLZ section line for line
+after the rename (199 lines), all code before it is identical, and the KLZH section differs only by the `kzh_parse`
+hook. `src/algo/khuf.c` and the word decoder are the lane's files unchanged.
+
+## 2. Compatibility
+
+    sh benchmark/review40/klzh2/e2e.sh build/kolmo RC3/build/kolmo SCRATCH results/e2e-w4.tsv DATA/silesia/* DATA/enwik8_10m
+
+13 files, `-T 1`, the rc3 binary built from `5071f388`:
+
+| frames | written by | read by | result |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| default coders, `speed` and `balanced` | this build | — | byte-identical to the rc3 binary's (26 of 26) |
+| `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz`, `speed` (codec 28 blocks) | rc3 | this build | decode, `cmp` equal (13 of 13) |
+| `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz`, `balanced` (codec 29) | rc3 | this build | decode (13 of 13) |
+| `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz`, `balanced` (codec 29, wave-4 parse) | this build | rc3 | decode (13 of 13): same format, other bytes |
+| `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz`, `speed` (codec 31) | this build | rc3 | refused (13 of 13), as any unknown codec id |
+| `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz2` (codec 32, and 31 in `speed`) | this build | rc3 | refused (26 of 26) |
+
+All 78 frames written by this build decode to their input. Unit level (`make check-native`, ASan/UBSan): 15 blocks
+written by the rc3 sources for codecs 28 and 29 must decode (`tests/klz_rc3_frames.h`, printed by
+`tests/klz_rc3_emit.c` built against rc3); codec 28's writer is still pinned to rc3's bytes
+(`tests/klz_rc3_hashes.h`); KLZS runs in the round-trip, truncation and corrupt-payload loops.
+
+**Flagged:** under the opt-in, codec 29 now writes other bytes than rc3 did (the parse changed, the format did
+not), and the LZ4 roles write codec 31 instead of 28. No default output changes.
+
