+
+What the wave-4 parse does to codec 32:
+- **Level 3** (two tables, now with the second recent offset tried after each match): 69,115,455 -> 68,760,493
+  (-0.51%); against zstd -3 from -1.18% to **-1.69%**. nci goes from +2.61% to -2.06%, xml from +1.22% to -0.64%,
+  samba from +0.47% to -0.75%; x-ray (+0.38%) is the one file still above zstd -3.
+- **Level 1** (now one table of 6-byte keys): 71,541,209 -> 74,685,728 (**+4.40%**): the lane traded size for
+  parse speed at this level (codec 29: 73,541,314 -> 76,544,815). Against zstd -1 codec 32 is -3.52% (was -7.58%),
+  codec 29 -1.12% (was -5.00%). Whether level 1 should be the one-table parse is the lane's decision, kept as it
+  made it; rc3's two-table parse is what level 2 still is.
+- KLZS 3 (chains, lazy, 16-bit offsets): 85,991,219 bytes.
+
+Small blocks (xml + dickens + osdb, 25,623,410 bytes), 4 KiB / 32 KiB: KLZS 1 against LZ4 +6.16% / -0.44%
+(19,409,445 and 13,904,317 against 18,283,717 and 13,965,773); KLZH2 1 against zstd -1 +2.43% / -0.61%; KLZH2 3
+against zstd -3 +1.47% / +0.32% (raw: `results/w4small*-T1-*.txt`).
